<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  LaunchAgent for minirag-mcp serve: one HTTP server for every index in indexes.toml.

  Setup
  1. Install the command once with uv tool install, on the interpreter the server
     should run on (below); the README's "Running the server at login" has the line.
  2. Replace the placeholders: __MINIRAG__ (absolute path to the installed command,
     `command -v minirag-mcp`) and __HOME__ (your home directory). launchd expands
     neither ~ nor $HOME, so every path must be absolute. No version is written here:
     the server runs whatever `uv tool install` or `uv tool upgrade` installed.
  3. Copy this file to ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
  4. Start it:
       launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.minirag-mcp.plist
  5. Reload indexes.toml after editing it (host, port and token need a restart instead):
       launchctl kill HUP gui/$(id -u)/local.minirag-mcp
  6. After `uv tool upgrade minirag-mcp`, restart it on the new version:
       launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/local.minirag-mcp
  7. Stop it:
       launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/local.minirag-mcp

  The token is in ~/.config/minirag/token. Logs go to ~/Library/Logs/minirag-mcp.log.

  The [ocr] extra reads scanned PDFs and images; without it a sync fails each of them.
  On macOS it also installs Apple Vision's bindings, the second reader of unsure pages.

  Why the interpreter matters: macOS privacy (TCC) grants access to Documents,
  Desktop and similar folders per binary, and a LaunchAgent cannot ask for it. The
  installed command runs on the interpreter uv tool install was given: give that
  interpreter access to the folders you index, otherwise the sync sees them as empty or
  unreadable. A background process also cannot
  trigger the download of online-only files in cloud-synced folders (it fails with
  errno 11), so keep those folders set to "Always Keep on This Device". After the first
  start, run a real sync and verify that the counts are above zero and that no root is
  reported as held.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>local.minirag-mcp</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__MINIRAG__</string>
    <string>serve</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <dict>
    <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
    <false/>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/minirag-mcp.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/minirag-mcp.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
